content:
Days past due add to the late charge rate on a deduction schedule of a Paystride Earned Wage Access Program Agreement that a returned remittance reinstated. They are counted in calendar days from the schedule's original due date to today:

- 30 days or more: 0.5 percentage points are added;
- at least 10 but fewer than 30 days: 0.25 percentage points are added;
- fewer than 10 days: none.

The original due date is the due date recorded on the deduction schedule, not the date of the return.

Cases (hypothetical): a schedule originally due 34 calendar days before today takes 0.5 points even where its remittance came back only last week; one due 30 days before today takes 0.5; one due 12 days before today takes 0.25; one due 9 days before today takes none.
